From c4974497112cc2d5cf53e880a3a666555706fd61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 18:17:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07263/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-WMTE-5722/5723:
 generator-swap induction-floor test (Gemma-4-31B/12B) -- clean NULL

Tests whether a stronger SOTA generator (Gemma-4-31B-it / -12B-it) breaks the
world-model induction floor where the frozen Qwen3.5-9B-MTP scores heldout=0.0.
Same REQ-ARC-WMTE-5720 actions-to-progress harness, 6-game roster, seeded level-up
windows, frozen/codeonly arm so the generator is the only variable, GPU 1.

Result (36 cells, all re-run under the attribution fix, every cell carries
induce_ok): clean NULL. heldout_accuracy floored at 0.0 for all three generators;
ZERO real level-ups. Gemma-31B induces reliably (11/12) but no better than the 9B
on exact-match (only a modest non-significant cell_recall edge, p=0.625).
Gemma-12B FAILS to induce on 11/12 cells -- worse than the 9B, not "~ 31B".
Recommendation: KEEP the frozen live default (operator-only); capacity is not the
binding lever on this induction path.

Also commits the corrected artifacts + the preserved pre-fix (buggy-harness) run as
a record: the pre-fix run's apparent Gemma "floor-move" cells were stale re-reads /
small-N noise that did not replicate under clean attribution (see the artifacts'
attribution_integrity block; harness fix + regression test in the prior commit's
arc_actions_to_progress change, folded in here).

